    "body": "Work landed locally on issue/74-gpu-adapter-selection (c14a93f), gating now before push:\n- GPU startup lists and logs every adapter (`gpu: seen ...` lines), then tries them one by one - your `--gpu <name>` / `CAMCRAFT_GPU` choice, the high-performance pick, discrete before integrated, the native API (DX12 on Windows) before Vulkan - configuring the surface from what it reports (format, Fifo vsync, alpha) instead of assuming; a failure names the adapter and reason and moves on; if none works, a dialog lists every adapter tried and why.\n- Frames over 100 ms log one `gpu: slow frame ...` line naming the slowest phase.\n- Stall cause not found headlessly: nothing on the idle frame path blocks. Leading suspect: Vulkan on an Optimus laptop copying every frame from the Quadro to the Intel chip that drives the display - DX12-first should avoid it. This stays open (Refs, not Fixes) until the reporter's log confirms.\n\n**For the reporter, once this ships**: the startup `gpu:` lines, the `gpu: slow frame` line while orbiting on the P3200, and whether `--gpu-backend dx12` or `--gpu quadro` changes the lag.",
