    "body": "claimed: main session (review fixes for PR #76) · 2026-11-07T13:41Z · branch issue/74-gpu-adapter-selection · plan: the independent review found (1) a lost device during configure passes as success (only a Validation error scope; OOM/Internal go to wgpu's panicking handler) - push OOM/Internal scopes and detect device loss; (2) same-GPU matching across backends by name can put Vulkan ahead of DX12 - match by PCI vendor/device id; (3) the refusal omits skipped adapters; plus the View3D pipeline failure on the chosen adapter neither tries the next adapter nor shows the dialog - likely the 'Intel never renders' spot.",
