    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T13:58:32Z",
    "body": "Review fixes landed locally (cd35ee1), gating now:\n- each adapter now goes through configure, the 3D view build and one test frame (acquire, clear, submit, present) inside Validation, OutOfMemory and Internal error scopes, with a device-lost flag and a 5 s poll - any failure (including a lost device, which used to pass silently) fails that adapter by name and the next is tried;\n- the same GPU on DX12 and Vulkan is matched by PCI vendor/device id, so DX12 stays first even when the two drivers name it differently;\n- a 3D view pipeline failure now tries the next adapter, and if all fail the named dialog lists what was tried and what was skipped (it used to exit silently - the likeliest 'Intel never renders' spot);\n- `--gpu=name` / `--gpu-backend=name` forms parsed.\nNot run on hybrid hardware - the reporter's log remains the proof.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
