    "body": "Report from another hybrid laptop (helps narrow the lag half). Windows 11, Intel Iris Xe (0x8086/0x46a6) + NVIDIA RTX 3050 Ti Laptop (0x10de/0x25a0). Drivers: NVIDIA 32.0.16.1074, Intel 32.0.101.7088. Running the v0.17.0 win-x64 portable.\n\n**Default run — selection works, no lag:**\n\n```\ngpu: seen \"Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics\" vendor 0x8086 device 0x46a6 integrated via vulkan\ngpu: seen \"NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Ti Laptop GPU\" vendor 0x10de device 0x25a0 discrete via vulkan\ngpu: seen \"Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics\" vendor 0x8086 device 0x46a6 integrated via dx12\ngpu: seen \"NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Ti Laptop GPU\" vendor 0x10de device 0x25a0 discrete via dx12\ngpu: seen \"Microsoft Basic Render Driver\" vendor 0x1414 device 0x008c cpu via dx12\ngpu: using \"NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Ti Laptop GPU\" via dx12 (discrete; Bgra8UnormSrgb Fifo Opaque)\n```\n\nAll 5 adapters enumerated, discrete-first + DX12-before-Vulkan picked correctly. Orbited an empty scene (no model) — smooth; loaded a model — still smooth. Zero `gpu: slow frame` lines for the entire session. Nothing analogous to problems (1)/(2) on this machine.\n\n**Forced-iGPU run — the Intel path is fine here too:** `--gpu \"Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics\"` → `gpu: using \"Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics\" via dx12 (integrated; ...)`; window rendered normally, rotate + pan smooth, again zero `gpu: slow frame` lines. So we can't reproduce the \"ends up on Intel and never renders\" symptom on this hybrid either.\n\nNet: the 1–2 s orbit lag and the Intel-adapter render failure both look specific to the Quadro P3200 path (or its driver), not to hybrid selection in general.\n",
